    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings stop rising abruptly at about 0.93–0.96 from 6 h onward, which looks like the reader saturating. To test this I diluted the 18 h aliquot. At 10× it read 0.478 (2 replicates), which works out to about 4.8. At 20× it read 0.225, which works out to about 4.5. The two dilutions roughly agree, so the reader responds about proportionally below 0.5. That puts the true OD at about 4.6, roughly five times the undiluted 0.92 reading. So the undiluted readings badly understate the late biomass."
